.TH TASKUI 1 "August 2026" "taskui" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
taskui \- folding, searchable front end for go\-task
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B taskui
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ DIR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B taskui
browses the Taskfile in
.IR DIR
(the current directory by default), runs tasks from it, and keeps their output
around to fold and search afterwards \(em both while a task is running and
across previous runs.
.PP
It requires
.BR task (1)
from https://taskfile.dev on
.BR PATH ;
everything it knows comes from asking go\-task rather than parsing Taskfiles
itself.
.PP
Existing Taskfile front ends are launchers: they pick a task, exit, and hand the
terminal over.
.B taskui
is meant to be the thing you sit in.
